From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 98/98] Count every encoded command for the launch timeline

Every command the encoder encodes is counted for the process's launch timeline
(caboose-bounded-memory/launch_timeline.h): its first instance, device, shader module and
pipeline, and the shader modules, pipelines and commands of each ten seconds of its first
fifteen minutes. The count is taken where the command profile already notes each command.
---
diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "caboose-bounded-memory/upload_cache.h"
 #include "caboose-bounded-memory/device_answers.h"
 #include "caboose-bounded-memory/one_way_start.h"
+#include "caboose-bounded-memory/launch_timeline.h"
 #include "caboose-bounded-memory/write_watch.h"
 #include "caboose-bounded-memory/static_query_cache.h"
 #include "caboose-bounded-memory/source_identity.h"
@@ -112,6 +113,7 @@ inline void reportLocked(bool atExit) {
     totals = Totals{};
 }
 inline void note(uint32_t opcode, uint32_t bytes) {
+    caboose::launch::command(opcode, bytes);  // the launch timeline, always (launch_timeline.h)
     if (!enabled()) return;
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mu);
     static const bool registered = [] {
